nd Aircraft Mechanics is in the related note, not applied. Hand to Hand: Basic, Expert for one related skill, Martial Arts or Assassin (if evil) for two. || RELATED: five at level one, one more at levels 3, 7 and 14. Espionage Wilderness Survival and Tracking only is Wilderness Survival and Tracking (people). Technical includes the Fanatic Robophile skill without the +10%, which needs the catalog row the Anti-Robot Specialist asks for. W.P. any but no specialized gunfighting skills from Rifts New West excludes W.P. Sharpshooting and W.P. Quick Draw. Secondary: four in total. || MONEY: 1D6x100 credits (text layer !D6xlOO) is starting_money; another 2D6x100 (text layer 2D6xlOO) in black market items is goods, in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT: Portable Scan Dihilator is the Rifts catalog row spelled Dihalator; the text layer reads FDD pocket audio recorder/player, and a render of printed 122 (cache p123) shows the page prints PDD, the catalog PDD pocket recorder row. NOT stored, no catalog row: black jumpsuit, street clothes (two sets), black paint stick, PDD-VC Pocket Digital Video Camera (440 stills or 45 minutes of video per disc), box of 100 disposable plastic gloves. Also not stored: one weapon per W.P. with four reloads, the full suit of personalized heavy and light environmental armor (printed that way; read as one of each, not stored), personal items. The Mode of Transportation table and the Cybernetic Implants proportions are in special_abilities; the implants are a spread across the class, not a fixed grant, so none is stored as a row."
---

## Lore

A Techno-Hound, or T-Hound, is a partial cyborg mercenary with a bottomless
appetite for technology. Robots are fine, but what this character really
loves is cybernetics, bionics, weapons and electronics. A T-Hound reads about
gadgets, then goes out to hunt, collect, trade, sell and repair them. The best
finds are advanced weapons, implants and relics from before the Rifts. Alien
devices are interesting but treated warily, and Techno-Wizardry is regarded
as an unpredictable thing best left alone, though a few own a piece or two.

Many are hoarders, and the worst of them cannot hear of a new development
without needing to own it. That hunger pulls them toward the places where
technology is thickest, such as Free Quebec, Upper Michigan and the Coalition
cities with their ''Burbs, because being far from the cutting edge is hard for
them to bear.

As a working soldier of fortune the T-Hound keeps to things small enough to
carry or stash, which in practice means a pack stuffed with tools, equipment
and gizmos. Plenty of them modify their gear or have it made to order, such
as boots and jackets with hidden compartments for weapons, picks and
circuitry. In the field they are the ones who can coax a dead machine back to
life for just long enough.

## GM Notes

Find Contraband is rolled at the stored figure when hunting bionics,
electronics and computers, and at -10% for every other kind of contraband.

Jury-Rig needs Mechanical Engineer and Electronics Engineer (-20% with only
Basic Electronics) and gives +5% to all Demolitions skills, Field Armorer,
Automotive Mechanics and Aircraft Mechanics. Roll the duration table in the
Jury-Rig Mechanics ability after each success. The Operator O.C.C. is the only
other class with this skill, and gets +6% on it.

The Fanatic Robophile skill may be taken as an O.C.C. Related Technical skill
at 50% +3% per level, without the Technical +10%; taking it halves the
character''s other mechanical and electronics bonuses (printed 118).

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: one weapon for each W.P. with four
full reloads (often Triax, Naruni or Bandito Arms), personalized environmental
armor of any kind, heavy and light, a black jumpsuit, two sets of street
clothes, a black paint stick, a PDD-VC Pocket Digital Video Camera, a box of
100 disposable plastic gloves and personal items.

Roll or assign the Mode of Transportation, and settle the character''s
cybernetics, from the abilities of those names.

Money: besides the credits, another 2D6x100 credits in black market items.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'headhunter-techno-hound');


